4,Nilo-Saharian languages - Sorosoro Sorosoro,https://www.sorosoro.org/en/nilo-saharian-languages/,"Surmic. Majang, Kwegu, Me’en, Mursi, Suri, Didinga, Narim, Murle, Tennet, Kacipo-Balesi.To appear. “Nilo-Saharan and its limits”. In Jean-Marie Hombert and Gerard Philippson (eds.), The Genetic Classification of African Languages Revisited.",Me’en,Nilo-Saharan
5,(PDF) Nilo-Saharan Languages,https://www.researchgate.net/publication/304040925_Nilo-Saharan_Languages,"Nilo-Saharan is essentially Greenberg's earlier Macro-Sudanic (or Chari-Nile) family, together with languages and language groups formerly assigned to historically isolated units.",Me’en,Nilo-Saharan
6,Comparing Nilo-Saharan East Africans And West Africans... | MedShun,https://medshun.com/article/are-nilo-saharan-east-africans-or-west-africans,"Nilo-Saharan East Africans are believed to have a closer genetic affinity to ancient hunter-gatherer populations, such as the Khoisan people of southern Africa. This is evidenced by the presence of unique DNA markers that are found predominantly in Nilo-Saharan populations.",Me’en,Nilo-Saharan
